<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CITIZEN BANK RAISES 100 MILLION RAND LOAN.</title>
<headline>CITIZEN BANK RAISES 100 MILLION RAND LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citizen Bank Ltd (CBL), a unit of Citizen Bank Holdings Ltd (CBH), said on Tuesday it had raised 100 million of secondary capital in the form of a five-year subordinated loan, compulsorily convertible into ordinary shares.</p>
<p>CBH has paid 43 million rand to acquire the right to receive the shares in CBL on conversion.</p>
<p>CBH also said it planned to change its name to FBC Holdings Ltd from April 1.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
